    "rendered_text": "<|im_start|>user\nSolve the following math problem. Make sure to put the answer (and only answer) inside \\boxed{}.\n\nFind \\[\\left|\\left(\\frac 35+\\frac 45i\\right)^6\\right|\\]<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nTo find $\\left|\\left(\\frac 35+\\frac 45i\\right)^6\\right|$, we'll use the fact that for any complex number $a+bi$, the absolute value of $a+bi$ is $\\left|a+bi\\right| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$.\n\nThe complex number here is $\\frac 35+\\frac 45i$, and we need to find its absolute value raised to the power of $6$. So, let's first find the absolute value of $\\frac 35+\\frac 45i$.\n\nApplying the formula for absolute value, we get:\n\\[ \\left|\\frac 35+\\frac 45i\\right| = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac 35\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac 45\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25} + \\frac{16}{25}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{25}} = \\sqrt{1} = 1 \\]\n\nNow, we need to raise this absolute value to the power of $6$.\n\\[ \\left|\\left(\\frac 35+\\frac 45i\\right)^6\\right| = \\left|\\frac 35+\\frac 45i\\right|^6 = 1^6 = \\boxed{1} \\]<|im_end|>",
