    "task": "math",
    "raw_problem": "The equation\n\\[(x - \\sqrt[3]{13})(x - \\sqrt[3]{53})(x - \\sqrt[3]{103}) = \\frac{1}{3}\\]has three distinct solutions $r,$ $s,$ and $t.$  Calculate the value of $r^3 + s^3 + t^3.$",
    "problem": "Solve the following math problem. Make sure to put the answer (and only answer) inside \\boxed{}.\n\nThe equation\n\\[(x - \\sqrt[3]{13})(x - \\sqrt[3]{53})(x - \\sqrt[3]{103}) = \\frac{1}{3}\\]has three distinct solutions $r,$ $s,$ and $t.$  Calculate the value of $r^3 + s^3 + t^3.$",
    "solution": "First, let's find the values of $r$, $s$, and $t$ by setting each factor equal to $0$:\n   \\begin{align*}\n   x - \\sqrt[3]{13} = 0 &\\Rightarrow x = \\sqrt[3]{13} = r \\\\\n   x - \\sqrt[3]{53} = 0 &\\Rightarrow x = \\sqrt[3]{53} = s \\\\\n   x - \\sqrt[3]{103} = 0 &\\Rightarrow x = \\sqrt[3]{103} = t \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n\nSince these are distinct solutions, we can use Vieta's formulas for the cubic equation, $x^3 - (r + s + t)x^2 + (rs + rt + st)x - rst = 0$.\n\nFrom Vieta's formulas we have:\n   \\begin{align*}\n   r + s + t &= -b \\\\\n   rs + rt + st &= c \\\\\n   rst &= -d\n   \\end{align*}\n\nExpanding the equation $(x - r)(x - s)(x - t) = 0$, we get:\n\\[ x^3 - (r + s + t)x^2 + (rs + rt + st)x - rst = 0 \\]\n\nComparing coefficients with the cubic equation we started with, we have:\n   \\begin{align*}\n   r + s + t &= 0 \\\\\n   rs + rt + st &= - \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\n   rst &= \\sqrt[3]{13} \\sqrt[3]{53} \\sqrt[3]{103} \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n\nNow we need to find $r^3 + s^3 + t^3$. Using the identity:\n\\[ (r + s + t)^3 = r^3 + s^3 + t^3 + 3(r + s + t)(rs + rt + st) - 3rst \\]\n\n\\[ 0^3 = r^3 + s^3 + t^3 + 3(0)(-\\frac{1}{3}) - 3 \\sqrt[3]{13} \\sqrt[3]{53} \\sqrt[3]{103} \\]\n\n\\[ r^3 + s^3 + t^3 = 3 \\sqrt[3]{13} \\sqrt[3]{53} \\sqrt[3]{103} = 3 \\sqrt[3]{13 * 53 * 103} = 3 \\sqrt[3]{70877} = 3 \\cdot 41 = \\boxed{170} \\]",
